cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  LC-Implicit-QAOA: Active-Workspace-Capped Exact
  Objective-and-Gradient Evaluation for Training over
  Bounded QUBO Light Cones
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to its results, please
  cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chih-Chung
    family-names: Hsu
    email: chihchung@nycu.edu.tw
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Smart Industry and Green Energy,
      National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University, Hsinchu, Taiwan
    website: 'https://cchsu.info'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jesse1029/lc-implicit-qaoa'
url: 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.05610'
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: 'arXiv:2608.05610'
    description: arXiv preprint
abstract: >-
  Exact objective and adjoint-gradient evaluation for QUBO-QAOA
  over bounded light cones. The evaluator profiles cone structure
  before allocation, jointly selects equal-size microbatches and
  checkpoint schedules under a named active-workspace byte budget,
  and rejects infeasible requests before any local-amplitude or
  workspace allocation. It materializes neither a global state nor
  a global cost table, so its cost is governed by cone cardinality
  rather than by qubit count.
keywords:
  - QAOA
  - QUBO
  - quantum simulation
  - light cone
  - adjoint differentiation
  - combinatorial optimization
